    "questionCode": "MH-9-MTH2-3-3.2.1-OSC-101",
    "text": "Which criterion proves two right-angled triangles congruent if the hypotenuse and one side of one triangle are congruent to the hypotenuse and corresponding side of the other?",
    "options": [
      {
        "text": "SSS test",
        "isCorrect": false
      },
      {
        "text": "AAA test",
        "isCorrect": false
      },
      {
        "text": "SAS test",
        "isCorrect": false
      },
      {
        "text": "Hypotenuse-Side test",
        "isCorrect": true
      }
    ],
    "correctAnswer": "D",
    "solution": "Step 1: Congruence requires identity in both shape and size.\nStep 2: Equal corresponding angles guarantee same shape, but side scale factor may vary.\nStep 3: Correct answer: Hypotenuse-Side test.",
