    "questionCode": "MH-9-MTH2-4-4.3.1-OSC-101",
    "text": "In constructing \\(\\triangle ABC\\) given its perimeter and base angles \\(\\angle B = 60^\\circ\\) and \\(\\angle C = 80^\\circ\\), what base angles are constructed on the perimeter line segment \\(XY\\)?",
    "options": [
      {
        "text": "\\(60^\\circ\\) and \\(80^\\circ\\)",
        "isCorrect": false
      },
      {
        "text": "\\(120^\\circ\\) and \\(160^\\circ\\)",
        "isCorrect": false
      },
      {
        "text": "\\(45^\\circ\\) and \\(45^\\circ\\)",
        "isCorrect": false
      },
      {
        "text": "\\(30^\\circ\\) and \\(40^\\circ\\) (half of the given base angles)",
        "isCorrect": true
      }
    ],
    "correctAnswer": "D",
    "solution": "Step 1: In perimeter construction, temporary baseline \\(XY = AB + BC + CA\\).\nStep 2: The angles at endpoints \\(X\\) and \\(Y\\) are drawn equal to half of \\(\\angle B\\) and half of \\(\\angle C\\).\nStep 3: Hence, the angles constructed are \\(\\frac{60^\\circ}{2} = 30^\\circ\\) and \\(\\frac{80^\\circ}{2} = 40^\\circ\\).",
